    "annotations": {
      "description": "The router itself adds microseconds; a p95 this high means the backend is slow or queueing. Compare with the app's own request duration before touching Traefik. Threshold is provisional: the busiest router averaged 76 ms on 2026-11-21, and the buckets were only widened that day, so re-tune after a week of real p95. Panel 'p95 and p99 latency by router' has the shape, and the 99th percentile separates 'one slow endpoint' from 'everything is slow'.",
      "summary": "Traefik router {{ $labels.router }} has a p95 above 1 s"
    },
    "condition": "C",
    "data": [
      {
        "datasourceUid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093",
        "model": {
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, router) (rate(traefik_router_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m]))) > 1) and on(router) (sum by (router) (rate(traefik_router_requests_total[5m])) > 0.01)",
